</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, October 25, 2004 - 10:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I MEANT TO SAY LINE 5 OF THE GRID, NOT LINE 6. <BR> <BR>SORRY, <BR> <BR>WICHITAN<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1279-->
<!--Post: 1280--><!--Time: 1098751240-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1280"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pilot<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pilot<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, October 25, 2004 - 5:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting.  I looked at it several times and here&#39;s what I got out of the circled letters:  The first set of course is BTK.  The second is UCL which may stand for uncle.  The third, DMV which is the Department of Motor Vehicles and the forth of course is Fox meaning Nancy Fox.  Is this a puzzle by BTK or just something trivial? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1280-->
<!--Post: 1291--><!--Time: 1098883644-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1291"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, October 27, 2004 - 6:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This grid in and of itself,I suggest,is not a puzzle but rather,a key.What we are looking at here is a basic system of Numerology. In any system of Numerology, the letters of the Alphabet respond to the 9 digits or single numbers.The letters of the Alphabet must be reduced &#40;Fadic reduction&#41;to single numbers, so consequently more than one letter responds to the same number as shown in this grid. <BR>All letters have numerical equations, therefore all combinations of letters in names respond to a certain numerical value. When a name is given to a person,city,or anything else, it lets loose a certain Occult force expressed in its numbers. <BR>At least that&#39;s the thinking behind it, for what it&#39;s worth. <BR>The system is very much akin to astrology and is used for a variety of operations designed at prediction such as Name number,Birth path number, destiny number,monthly number etc.Essentially, if you believe in this crap,you can plot a course to do things on days that are lucky for you,or a path that best suits/corresponds with the &#34;heavens&#34;.Of course it could also have been employed here to set up a link or puzzle. <BR> <BR>The letters BTK correspond with the second,the 20th and the 11th letters of the Alphabet. <BR>&#40;B=2&#41; &#40;T=20 = 2&#43;0 =2&#41;, &#40;K=11 = 1&#43;1=2&#41;. Hence they fall in with this grid with a value of 2 for each. <BR>  <BR>To attribute a Name number to BTK,it would be 2&#43;2&#43;2=6. <BR>Perhaps if we were to go back over names and dates we might see some connection develop. <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1291-->
<!--Post: 1292--><!--Time: 1098884999-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1292"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, October 27, 2004 - 6:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That&#39;s a FAIR assumption, but, what about 4 and 6?  This theory of yours can not be used for 4 and 6. <BR> <BR>wichitan<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1292-->
<!--Post: 1294--><!--Time: 1098889155-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1294"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, October 27, 2004 - 7:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Wichitan, <BR>          Don&#39;t know what you mean by &#34;it can not be used for four or six&#34; can you explain? <BR>The theory is that he may have used Numerology. <BR>Everything else is standard Numerology including that Gird,that&#39;s the layout.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
