<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1331"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, October 31, 2004 - 8:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The puzzle/code/key allegedly was included in a BTK correspondence. The original source of that info was a now deceased Wichita BTK detective; my source was someone who knew him. <BR> <BR>Since posting the puzzle/code/key, I&#39;ve received corroboration from a good source that, according to what he was told from another former BTK detective, it came from BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
