<!--Post: 1347--><!--Time: 1099509728-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1347"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Interested<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Interested<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, November 03, 2004 - 11:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok here is my theroy.I think that the zodiac and the btk are the same person.I think he moved from california to kansas and the grid represents the 2 on the top as his second spree.Just a theroy.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1347-->
<!--Post: 1354--><!--Time: 1099584275-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1354"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, November 04, 2004 - 8:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Sean--that pretty much settles it. <BR>I should have read all the threads before posting. <BR> <BR>So I have to agree with the others in asking...why? <BR> <BR>Why does the grid appear hand written with letters circled in red?  Red herring?  Or is this something that was sent by BTK?  Or is it just another of a million things that have the letters btk in it that we are wasting time with?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1354-->
<!--Post: 1355--><!--Time: 1099590609-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1355"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, November 04, 2004 - 9:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Clearly this grid was not constructed by BTK as it has been around for centuries,in many forms. <BR>We have one here but there are also Hebrew and Celtic versions. <BR>I don&#39;t know if the letters we actually circled in red or if Tom highlighted them. <BR>Tom says he believes it came from BTK, so we can only go with that.What he appears to be doing at the moment is offering clues. Again, we don&#39;t know whether these are genuine or fake. <BR>If genuine, I can only think it a clue to something else along Numerological lines. <BR>The other scenario is that came across this grid and acted on it BTK,DMV ,FOX etc.That seems far less likely in my view. <BR>As I said earlier BTK was once quoted as saying &#40;in relation to his victims&#41; that he &#34;took down their numbers and followed then home&#34;. <BR>Questions that spring to mind are <BR>What numbers was he referring to? <BR>If he meant addresses, then that&#39;s logical. <BR>If he meant phone numbers, why did he need them? <BR>Was it liscence plate numbers? <BR> <BR>Did these victims present him with some identification? <BR>Who knows? But I suppose there might be a possibility that he chose his victims using Numerology or perhaps there was/is some pattern there. Then again he may have already supplied us with numbers and this grid is some clue to that. <BR>This grid though does suggest Name/DOB etc as that&#39;s what it&#39;s used for. <BR>The list is endless until we have more information  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1355-->
<!--Post: 1356--><!--Time: 1099598902-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1356"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Doone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Doone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, November 04, 2004 - 12:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It a big compicated game my friend of the monster play putting victims number down, follow them, checking up on them waiting in the dark, waiting, waiting... the pressure is great and sometimes he run the game to his liking. Maybe you can stop him. I can&#39;t. He has aready chosen his next victim or victims. I don&#39;t who they are yet. The next day after I read the paper, I will know, but it to late. Good luck hunting. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1356-->
<!--Post: 1357--><!--Time: 1099621501-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1357"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, November 04, 2004 - 6:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Doone: <BR>Yeah...I read the Danny Rolling book too.....try something original. <BR> <BR>Sean, I understand the grid in question has been around for centuries.  I was referring to the fact that the version posted on the site is stylized as being hand written, both the numbers and the red circles. That&#39;s why i asked if it was from a letter or if somone just created it &#34;for effect.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1357-->
<!--Post: 1359--><!--Time: 1099633541-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1359"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Doone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Doone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, November 04, 2004 - 9:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Juno, I copy and pasted quotes from BTK&#39;s first letter from Oct. 1979. <BR>Was thinking it needed no explanation. <BR>I guess it did. <BR>But I am glad you read books.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1359-->
<!--Post: 1367--><!--Time: 1099670299-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1367"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, November 05, 2004 - 7:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wasn&#39;t picking you up on anything Juno, just explaining what you asked as,I saw it.That I mentioned that the grid was around for centuries was only my way of reinforcing the belief that it was a clue rather than the puzzle itself.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1367-->
<!--Post: 1371--><!--Time: 1099690530-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1371"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, November 05, 2004 - 1:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Doone--I apologize for being an ass. <BR> <BR>Sean--I agree with what you said.  I am just curious as to why the grid appears to be handwritten.  I guess tom just chose that particular font for effect.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1371-->
<!--Post: 1880--><!--Time: 1103071777-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1880"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brazilian<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brazilian<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 14, 2004 - 4:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that puzzle was send by BTK to inform that he would send Nancy Fox driver license as his next clue. <BR> <BR>In the puzzle we can clearly read BTK, CLU&#40;e&#41;, DMV &#40;or anything related, in this case, her driver license&#41; and FOX.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1880-->
<!--Post: 1897--><!--Time: 1103084058-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1897"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 14, 2004 - 8:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The puzzle was apparently originally sent by BTK quite a few years ago. However, I just published it less than two months ago. Interesting how BTK&#39;s latest drop just happens to involve FOX, DMV and CLU.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1897-->
<!--Post: 1907--><!--Time: 1103114787-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1907"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 4:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->And I felt like a moron after posting this above: <BR> <BR>&#34;I thought it meant  <BR> <BR>btk clu dmv new fox  <BR> <BR>Which can be rearanged several ways.  <BR> <BR>New BTK clu&#40;e&#41; fox dmv  <BR>Or maybe phonetically it means fox&#40;K&#41;new btk&#34;  <BR> <BR>Interesting anyway.&#34; <BR> <BR>At any rate, maybe he thought of it because this was on the board instead of the other way around.  BTK did not supply the grid, did he?  <BR>  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1907-->
<!--Post: 1972--><!--Time: 1103212230-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1972"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Inquisitive<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Inquisitive<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 7:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->What about line 1?  In the 70&#39;s through the 80&#39;s I believe that a criminal justice degree at WSU was AJS &#40;Administration of Justice Studies&#41;.  Maybe that was his major. Probably grasping though.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1972-->
<!--Post: 1980--><!--Time: 1103223360-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1980"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bodycheck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bodycheck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 10:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->in Chat last night Tom said he just posted it to see if there would be a response...that it IS NOT from BTK but just a common numerology grid &#40;which it is&#41; Tom said he highlighted those sections to see if anythihng would happen and wow..did it ever... <BR> <BR>B<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1980-->
<!--Post: 1984--><!--Time: 1103229783-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1984"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 12:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The police have never admitted the numerology key was included in a BTK letter. However, I was told it had and proceeded under that assumption. Since we don&#39;t know for sure BTK is into numerology, I treated the key like a simple word find.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1984-->
<!--Post: 1985--><!--Time: 1103229985-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1985"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 12:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom is in &#34;Control of All Things&#34; <BR>Apparently BTK reads the board. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1985-->
<!--Post: 1995--><!--Time: 1103239323-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1995"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 3:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I still think the grid was meant as a key for a puzzle BTK included in one of his letters.  However, that doesn&#39;t mean that he didn&#39;t decide to use it for something else at a later date, or that it had a double meaning the entire time.  For all we know, BTK was cruising this site, saw what Tom did with it, and thought, &#34;Way cool! I hadn&#39;t intended that, but it&#39;s a great idea!  That&#39;s what I&#39;ll do next!&#34; and so now we have a new <b>BKT clu</b> that includes the <b>DMV</b> license for <b>Fox</b>...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1995-->
<!--Post: 2012--><!--Time: 1103244810-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2012"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 4:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->So it&#39;s likely that BTK included it in one of the &#34;original&#34; letters, as opposed to the current letters?  That is what i gather at least, and that this is either coincidental or Tom is controlling him!  <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2012-->
